      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:f0337cf1bfccd6c53bc439508e51b90faf9a2f78e38621d151c8707d43fcce52\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:a389b8fed743e509d0dcad33b58b44df005d2dcfc56f91c16946fe38f5d51c94\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:c9e9e050a17c97579231e63c43f02d32300106bd40f3e8b96fe37f5d6d8f7a98\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:592f3013b938ff106d52a99a649b33864350569b3e7e9cc206b49147263c1cc3\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3819c2c46469f21520e785a70c733ff0dcab1e188f1adf6373abd929df856816\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[],\"defined_terms\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":965,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":292,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A304211a283f94602359614639e26b9072acdf8e47389f75e2261abed914de7c3:0:292:sha256-006ed0c3aae91eac183598f171ac8cdd6b08140e159c0683f247bafcb49be64e\",\"quote\":\"(b) In making such determination the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides, shall deem any person qualified to serve on grand and petit juries in the district court unless he—\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":965,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A304211a283f94602359614639e26b9072acdf8e47389f75e2261abed914de7c3:294:965:sha256-fb4e93d7387d50b5cc110965a6b0991676bc497e24b50b36d91b6c08f1edd257\",\"quote\":\"(1) is not a citizen of the United States eighteen years old who has resided for a period of one year within the judicial district;\\n\\n(2) is unable to read, write, and understand the English language with a degree of proficiency sufficient to fill out satisfactorily the juror qualification form;\\n\\n(3) is unable to speak the English language;\\n\\n(4) is incapable, by reason of mental or physical infirmity, to render satisfactory jury service; or\\n\\n(5) has a charge pending against him for the commission of, or has been convicted in a State or Federal court of record of, a crime punishable by imprisonment for more than one year and his civil rights have not been restored.\",\"start\":294},{\"end\":191,\"field\":\"actor\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A304211a283f94602359614639e26b9072acdf8e47389f75e2261abed914de7c3:33:191:sha256-2498fc9b69da8054343d8fc231c4a25c30a71919d30eedda0ade9e8eda321d86\",\"quote\":\"the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides\",\"start\":33},{\"end\":198,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A304211a283f94602359614639e26b9072acdf8e47389f75e2261abed914de7c3:193:198:sha256-56ee5b508706bf2de91712d85d6d1e11ddbff01949142ed6e8c22e3b1bed1c71\",\"quote\":\"shall\",\"start\":193},{\"end\":292,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A304211a283f94602359614639e26b9072acdf8e47389f75e2261abed914de7c3:0:292:sha256-006ed0c3aae91eac183598f171ac8cdd6b08140e159c0683f247bafcb49be64e\",\"quote\":\"(b) In making such determination the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides, shall deem any person qualified to serve on grand and petit juries in the district court unless he—\",\"start\":0}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:f898db4e588bc75c3000d81bbe47fcf7fe1f7b3d994202e8522b087622408503\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3819c2c46469f21520e785a70c733ff0dcab1e188f1adf6373abd929df856816\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"shall\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:251cbe73ea92273f4adf12656308ef124648a4e546f31f881bab5194ada6dfab\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(b) In making such determination the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides, shall deem any person qualified to serve on grand and petit juries in the district court unless he—\\n\\n(1) is not a citizen of the United States eighteen years old who has resided for a period of one year within the judicial district;\\n\\n(2) is unable to read, write, and understand the English language with a degree of proficiency sufficient to fill out satisfactorily the juror qualification form;\\n\\n(3) is unable to speak the English language;\\n\\n(4) is incapable, by reason of mental or physical infirmity, to render satisfactory jury service; or\\n\\n(5) has a charge pending against him for the commission of, or has been convicted in a State or Federal court of record of, a crime punishable by imprisonment for more than one year and his civil rights have not been restored.\",\"references\":[],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:8ba56c534df094f12d2ab2e70b71832c442a5c765d6527e302c01db36119516a\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(b) In making such determination the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides, shall deem any person qualified to serve on grand and petit juries in the district court unless he—\"],\"scope_text\":\"In making such determination\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":0,\"summary\":\"In making the determination, the chief judge of the district court, or such other district court judge as the plan may provide, or the clerk if the court’s jury selection plan so provides, must deem any person qualified to serve on grand and petit juries in the district court unless the person: (1) is not a citizen of the United States eighteen years old who has resided for a period of one year within the judicial district; (2) is unable to read, write, and understand the English language with a degree of proficiency sufficient to fill out satisfactorily the juror qualification form; (3) is unable to speak the English language; (4) is incapable, by reason of mental or physical infirmity, to render satisfactory jury service; or (5) has a charge pending against him for the commission of, or has been convicted in a State or Federal court of record of, a crime punishable by imprisonment for more than one year and his civil rights have not been restored.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"term_refs\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
